^[chapter/14/sections][
  s01: {
    handle: "section/01"
    type: "section"
    title: "The Wrong Quiet"
    excerpt: "Dawn smelled of frost and wet fur, and of nothing else at all. Boof put her nose to the ground and read the field the way she read it every morning. Frost on the furrows. Loam under the frost. The berry rows asleep be..."
    route: ^[chapter/14/s01]{open}
  }
  s02: <
    handle: "custom-boof/02"
    type: "custom-boof"
    excerpt: "Boof did not keep a week. She kept mornings. Each one came with its own smell and she took it as it came. A person has to be told what day it is. A dog only has to be there. So she did not know it was Thursday. She di..."
    route: ^[chapter/14/s02]{open}
  >
  s03: <
    handle: "custom-boonberry/03"
    type: "custom-boonberry"
    excerpt: "The berries noticed first. They always did; noticing is most of what a boonberry is for. Every morning since the wish, the little lights under the ice had leaned toward the warm furrow, the way a sleeper turns to the ..."
    route: ^[chapter/14/s03]{open}
  >
  s04: {
    handle: "section/04"
    type: "section"
    title: "The Hat Above the Furrow"
    excerpt: "The warm furrow was steaming when she reached it. It always steamed now. That was the wish: one furrow kept open, always, for whatever arrived next. The frost drew back from it in a soft margin, and beneath it the ant..."
    route: ^[chapter/14/s04]{open}
  }
  s05: <
    handle: "custom-boof/05"
    type: "custom-boof"
    excerpt: "She went to see what he was looking at, because that is what a dog does with somebody else's attention. It was an ant. One ant, at the very end of the ruled street, holding up a torch that had gone out. It held it the..."
    route: ^[chapter/14/s05]{open}
  >
